# CI & Ontrack CLI
/.ontrack-cli*

# Local Casc configuration
/casc


# `build` above is unanchored, so it matches every directory called `build` anywhere in the
# tree - including source directories that have nothing to do with a Gradle output. Each one
# has to be re-included by name, and the *directory* itself has to be: git never descends into
# an excluded directory, so negating a file inside one does nothing.
#
# The failure is silent in the worst way - the files exist on disk, the app runs, the tests
# pass, and `git status` shows nothing - so a new one is only noticed once a fresh checkout
# cannot build.
#
# The net.nemerosa.ontrack.build *package* under buildSrc:
!buildSrc/src/main/kotlin/net/nemerosa/ontrack/build/
!buildSrc/src/test/kotlin/net/nemerosa/ontrack/build/
# The mobile UI's build screen, which is a route named after the entity it shows:
!ontrack-web-core/app/mobile/build/

# Local development stack state (scripts/dev-stack.sh)
.yontrack-dev/
# Integration test stack state (ItStack in buildSrc)
.yontrack-it/
# KDSL acceptance stack state (KdslStack in buildSrc)
.yontrack-kdsl/

# Kotlin compiler daemon session files
.kotlin/

# Local MCP server configuration, written by the IDE and pointing at a port on this machine
.mcp.json
